id: pm-95h7pg
title: "The gate contributors run before merging fails on every Claude Code workstation and passes on the runner for the same tree, because a harness probe writes advisory warnings into the surface the token budget measures"
description: "pnpm quality:static runs pnpm quality:token-budget, which measures pm health --check-only inside a sandboxed fixture and compares it to a committed baseline of 152 tokens / 604 bytes. On this workstation the measured output is 267 tokens / 1066 bytes and the gate blocks. On the hosted runner the same tree passes; CI run 31938652077 on main reports Gates (static) success. The difference is two advisory health warnings, provenance_resolver_zero_success:claude-code:model:claude_session_file:12 and the matching version row, emitted because the host process is a Claude Code session and the claude_session_file resolver is attempted once per fixture item inside a sandbox that has no session file. The gate already sets PM_AUTHOR explicitly, which does not suppress harness probing."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:ci","area:provenance",gate-parity,local-hosted-divergence,token-budget
created_at: "2026-08-16T11:03:54.902Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-16T11:04:32.160Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: "The token-budget gate's measured surfaces do not vary with the harness running the suite, proven by a control that sets each supported harness's signal environment and asserts the verdict is unchanged; A resolver that cannot succeed in a sandbox because the sandbox has no session artifact does not raise a per-item advisory warning into a measured surface, or health's measured projection excludes advisory findings and the exclusion is declared; The local and hosted invocation of quality:token-budget produce the same verdict for the same tree, asserted rather than observed; The neutralization covers every harness signal the detector reads, not only the ambiguous foreign one, closing the gap between pm-xgah3a's first acceptance criterion and what its fix delivered"
parent: pm-33cw
risk: high
confidence: high
expected_result: A contributor running the mandated pre-merge gate on a clean checkout of main gets the same verdict CI gets.
actual_result: "The gate blocks on any Claude Code workstation and passes in CI, for a reason unrelated to token budgets."
dependencies[2]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
